1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,450
Your cat isn't just making biscuits on you.

2
00:00:02,490 --> 00:00:04,910
It's doing one of the first things it ever learned.

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:07,980
Newborn kittens knead their mother's belly while they nurse,

4
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,910
and the pressing helps the milk flow.

5
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,170
Most cats never grow out of it.

6
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:13,990
When they feel safe and warm,

7
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:15,450
the kitten move comes back,

8
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,910
often with purring, and sometimes drool.

9
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,100
They have scent glands between their toes,

10
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:23,010
so every press leaves a little of their smell on you.

11
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,190
You've been claimed.

12
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:25,230
And the claws?

13
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:26,790
Kittens do that too.

14
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,960
Their mom just had more fur than you.

15
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:31,980
So if your cat climbs on your lap and starts kneading,

16
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:32,930
hold still, because
